new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..dc921510bc
--- /dev/null
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommax/patches-6.12/0918-net-dsa-realtek-rtl8365mb-add-sgmii-hsgmii-support.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,604 @@
+From: OpenWrt
+Date: Tue, 7 Jul 2026 20:00:00 +0200
+Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: realtek: rtl8365mb: add SGMII and HSGMII support
+
+The mainline rtl8365mb driver only configures RGMII on the extension
+interface, so switches such as the RTL8367S that are connected to the SoC
+over a (2.5G) SGMII/HSGMII link cannot be brought up (phylink_mac_config
+is a no-op for non-RGMII and SGMII/2500BASEX are not advertised).
+
+Add SGMII and HSGMII (advertised as 2500BASE-X) support for extension
+interface 1. The SerDes calibration tables are taken from the GPL-2.0
+Realtek vendor driver that already lives in OpenWrt's mediatek target
+(rtl8367c_setAsicPortExtMode). Unlike the vendor driver, no 8051 SerDes
+firmware is needed: the vendor firmware acts as a runtime babysitter for
+the SerDes, and bring-up works without it as long as the SerDes in-band
+SGMII autoneg is disabled and the link parameters are forced (verified
+on hardware: full 2.5G trunk operation, NAT throughput included).
+
+The SDS_MISC force bits (link/speed/duplex/pause) and the SGMII in-band
+autoneg disable are both mandatory - each alone leaves a link-up trunk
+that passes no traffic (verified live on AX55 hardware).
+
+This is a re-derivation of Hauke Mehrtens' 2022 netdev series, minus the
+firmware blob whose licensing blocked it back then.
+
+Needed for the TP-Link Archer AX55 v1 (IPQ5018 + RTL8367S).
+
+Rebased onto the v7.2 backports (942-xx) that split rtl8365mb.c into
+rtl8365mb.c and rtl8365mb_l2.c.
+
+Signed-off-by: OpenWrt <noreply@openwrt.org>
+---
+
+Cold-boot reliability: poll the SDS status from the CPU port MIB work: verify the
+SerDes RX is locked (SDS status 0x3D) and pulse the vendor's
+SerDes reset from the CPU port MIB poll until it does - this replaces the 8051 firmware's
+babysitter loop for the one case where it matters.
+
+--- a/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/rtl8365mb.c
++++ b/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/rtl8365mb.c
+@@ -207,6 +207,38 @@
+ #define RTL8365MB_EXT_PORT_MODE_1000X_100FX	11
+ #define RTL8365MB_EXT_PORT_MODE_1000X		12
+ #define RTL8365MB_EXT_PORT_MODE_100FX		13
++/* Registers used to bring up the (H)SGMII extension interface. The
